<!DOCTYPE html>
{# The document's language, so screen readers and browser translation
   follow the same choice the person made (XIV-8). #}
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale }}">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8">
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
		<title>{% block title %}Xivi{% endblock %}</title>
		{# The installation's own mark when it has one (XIV-48), and the generation
		   drawn as text when it has not — which is what a fresh clone shows. No
		   `type`: the deployment chooses the format, and a wrong one stated here
		   is worse than none stated at all. #}
		{% if chrome.logo %}
			<link rel="icon" href="{{ asset(chrome.logo) }}">
		{% else %}
			<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 16 16%22><text y=%2214%22>17</text></svg>">
		{% endif %}

		{# Bootstrap does not follow the operating system's setting on its own, and
		   this has to run before the body paints or the page flashes white. #}
		<script>
			document.documentElement.dataset.bsTheme =
				window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
		</script>

		{% block stylesheets %}{% endblock %}
		{% block javascripts %}{{ importmap('app') }}{% endblock %}
	</head>
	<body class="bg-body-tertiary d-flex flex-column min-vh-100">
		{% block body %}{% endblock %}

		{#
			Which version you are looking at. The first question about any bug
			report, and the one nobody can answer from memory.

			**A block rather than a fixed footer**, because the login page wants the
			version and not the furniture around it (XIV-79). It is a single centred
			card on an otherwise empty page, and a bar pinned to the bottom-left
			corner of it read as a piece of the application that had wandered in from
			somewhere the visitor is not yet allowed to go. It overrides this with
			nothing and prints the version inside the card instead.

			The alternative was a second base template for signed-out pages, which is
			what was asked for. It was not taken: this file is almost entirely
			`<head>` — the favicon rule (XIV-48), the pre-paint theme script, the
			importmap — and a copy of it is a copy of all three. The theme script in
			particular must not drift between two files, because the failure mode is a
			page that flashes white and nobody notices which of the two copies stopped
			matching. One block buys the same thing and duplicates nothing.

			When a genuinely separate signed-out layout is wanted — a marketing page,
			a landing page (XIV-65) — that is the moment to split, and the split should
			put the `<head>` in a shared parent rather than copying it here.
		#}
		{% block footer %}
			<footer class="container page-shell mt-auto py-3">
				<p class="text-body-secondary small mb-0">Xivi {{ app_version }}</p>
			</footer>
		{% endblock %}
	</body>
</html>
